// Naming several targets places a box against the region that bounds them all.

box one    "first"
box two    "second"                 below one
box three  "third with a longer label"  below two

// A direction clears the furthest of them. This note says nothing about its own
// vertical position — that comes from the region.
note spans  "level with all three, and clear of the widest"  right of one and three  wrap: 24  gap: wide

// An alignment uses the region as a position. "top" is its top edge, not its middle.
note tops   "top level with the second box"                  right of two  top level with two  wrap: 20  gap: tight

box beside  "centered on the top two"  right of spans  level with one and two  gap: wide
